      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-414",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Splitting up the integral into the difference of two integrals and evaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4}-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sec}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\operatorname{sec}\u20610)-(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\operatorname{sin}\u20610) \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{2}-1)-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
