        {
          "question": "e-415",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Splitting up the sum and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(2{x}^{3}-5)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{-2}^{2}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}{|}_{-2}^{2}-5x{|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{-2}^{2}-5x\\,{|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{4}-(-2)^{4})-5(2-(-2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(16-16)-5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
